cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Counterfactual Shadow Control (CSC)"
message: "If you use this software or its experimental artifacts, please cite the accompanying paper once published."
type: software
# The creator list of the software archive is separate metadata from the paper's
# author list: it names who contributed to the code and the data, which is not
# automatically everyone on the manuscript. Decide each entry deliberately.
authors:
  - family-names: Tarasov
    given-names: Nikita
    affiliation: "Lviv Polytechnic National University"
    # orcid: TODO -- required by IEEE for all manuscript authors; also add here
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Dev-Nikita/csc-iot"
# The archive identifier a reader can actually open. The concept DOI
# 10.5281/zenodo.23165224 is registered but did not resolve in a browser on
# 2026-10-16, so it is not published anywhere.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23321904"
version: "0.3"
abstract: >-
  Uncertainty-aware proactive self-healing for mobile edge IoT systems.
  Evaluates action-conditioned counterfactual futures before intervening,
  executes the cheapest action satisfying a calibrated risk bound, abstains
  when none does, and validates counterfactual rankings by deterministic
  fork-and-replay of a distributed emulation testbed.
